/*
 * threat-detector  —  multi-page, receive-only wireless threat monitor
 *                     for the Heltec WiFi LoRa 32 (V3), ESP32-S3.
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * LISTEN-ONLY detection. The device NEVER transmits attack traffic (no deauth,
 * beacons, probe responses, or jamming). The only thing it transmits is your
 * own incident alerts over LoRa to your base station (opt-in, ENABLE_LORA).
 *
 * Press the PRG / USER button (GPIO 0) to cycle pages:
 *   1. DEAUTH        - deauth/disassoc flood detection (per-BSSID baseline)
 *   2. WIFI JAM      - RF-flood / interference heuristic (frame-rate collapse/spike)
 *   3. EVIL PORTAL   - OPEN bait APs + evil twins of your SSIDs
 *   4. BLE SPAM      - BLE advertisement flood (ENABLE_BT)
 *   5. SUBGHZ JAM    - sub-GHz RSSI jam detection via SX1262 (ENABLE_LORA)
 *   6. SUBGHZ BRUTE  - sub-GHz burst/brute-force listener via SX1262 (ENABLE_LORA, WIP)
 *   7. WIFI BRUTE    - auth/assoc flood (possible brute force / MDK-style attack)
 *
 * Alerts show on the OLED + Serial, and (ENABLE_LORA) are sent over LoRa.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * BUILD STATUS / HONEST NOTES:
 *   - Pages 1-4 and 7 (WiFi + BLE) are implemented and testable now.
 *   - Pages 5-6 and the LoRa uplink use the SX1262 via the RadioLib library.
 *     They are OFF by default so this compiles with no extra library. To enable:
 *       1) Library Manager -> install "RadioLib" by Jan Gromes.
 *       2) Set ENABLE_LORA to 1 below. Set your region frequency (LORA_FREQ).
 *     Sub-GHz detection is heuristic and needs on-hardware tuning per band.
 *   - Setup: board "Heltec WiFi LoRa 32(V3)" / "ESP32S3 Dev Module",
 *     Tools -> USB CDC On Boot -> Enabled. Needs the "U8g2" library.
 */

